    "details": {
      "alignment": "Neutral Good",
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "toad"
      },
      "cr": 0,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Liberated Toads cohort sheet — Barrel Survivor.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-liberated-toads-actors.py</code> from the Pond Patrol docket (<code>data/liberatedToadsSystem.json</code>, snapshot Highsun 24, 1040 BF): level 1 on the docket → CR 0 as commoner (ordinary toads without specialized training, but with potential); no armour (AC 10), hit points 1d6. A GM-ready reading of the docket, not a filed stat line; the docket stays the authority.</p><p><strong>Barrel Survivors</strong> — The original 150 trafficked toads - the heart of the movement. Leader: Elder Mudcap. The traumatized survivors of the barrel trafficking operation. Many still bear psychological and physical scars. They are the reason the Liberated Toads exist.</p><p><strong>Stands in for</strong> 54 docket rows (levels 1, 2, 3): Barrel survivor, Quiet majority, Bunk neighbor, Roll-call answer, Floor scrub, Blanket fold, Lamp lighter, Vest mender, Button sew, Cap care, Ward visitor, Assembly attendee. Rename the token for the toad at the table.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Specialisations</strong> — Testimony, Unity, Moral authority (the cohort feat)</li><li><strong>Commoner</strong> — classDefinitions.commoner: Survivor's Instinct (L1)</li><li><strong>Status</strong> — recovering: Many still traumatized; 3 confirmed deceased</li></ul>",
        "public": ""
      },
